      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Initially, the appointment approval form is sent."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening clause implicitly triggers the process start and describes the first action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After that, the approval is received."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the reception step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Following the approval, there is a contact with TS to clarify the timing."
      ],
      "justification": "Exact match for the clarification step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the approval is received, it is checked."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly supports the initial approval check action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "guard:b1->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the resource is internal, the appointment is authorized."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional implies the XOR branch and positive guard. Modeling the condition as an action node alongside the authorization step faithfully restates the source."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the resource is external, the appointment is also authorized."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the negative guard and corresponding action. The implied rejoining of the internal/external paths supports the converge node."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After the approval, the mandatory documentation along with the approval is sent to HR services."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the documentation submission step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The form is then scanned and recorded into the GovSource system."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for the scanning and recording step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11",
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The approval is checked and then sent along with the mandatory documentation to HR services."
      ],
      "justification": "Supports the repeated check and send actions described in the text."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n13",
        "action:n20"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "HR services receive the documentations and this marks the end of the process."
      ],
      "justification": "Describes the final reception action and explicitly signals the process termination."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n14",
        "guard:b2->n15",
        "action:n15"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If there are no variations, the process continues."
      ],
      "justification": "The conditional implies the branch and negative guard. Action nodes modeling the check and continuation align with the source."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n17",
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if there are variations, a business case is completed and attached."
      ],
      "justification": "Maps to the positive guard and action for the attachment step, matching the second textual repetition."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b3->n18",
        "action:n18"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if there are variations, a business case is completed."
